course: dictionary
lesson: 8462
title: What is a salary?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A salary is the money a person is paid for their job. Adults earn it by working, and it pays for a home, food and bills. When you read the word, look for clues in the words around it.
explain: «Adults earn money by working, and their salary pays for the home, food and bills.» The clues are earn, working and pays for. So a salary must be money that comes from work.
explain: «A salary is yearly pay; an hourly rate is pay for each hour worked.» Here the word salary is compared with pay for each hour. A salary is a fixed amount for the whole year, not a payment for each hour.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Put "the money a person is paid for their job" in place of salary, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A salary is the money a person is paid for their job.
fact: «A wage or salary is the money a worker is paid for their work.»
fact: A salary is usually a fixed amount for the year, split into monthly payments.
fact: Wages are usually paid by the hour or the week, so more hours means more pay.
fact: Useful phrases: earn a salary, a high salary, a yearly salary, salary per month.
exercise: «Adults earn money by working, and their salary pays for the home, food and bills.» What does salary mean? | A bill from the shop | *The money a person is paid for their job | A house where people live | A holiday away from work
exercise: «A salary is yearly pay; an hourly rate is pay for each hour worked.» Which one is pay for each hour worked? | A salary | A yearly bill | A career | *An hourly rate
exercise: Ravi says a salary is paid every hour. Is he right? | Yes, but only on Fridays | Yes, salaries are always paid every hour | *No, a salary is a fixed amount for the year, split into monthly payments | No, a salary is money you find on the street
test: What do adults use a salary to pay for? | Sweets for the whole street | Only their school fees | *The home, food and bills | Their holidays on the moon
test: Which phrase means a fixed amount of pay for the year? | Weekly bills | Lost wages | *A yearly salary | Hourly rate
exam: Which sentence uses salary correctly? | The salary of the dog is brown and soft | *Her salary arrives in her bank account every month | She went to salary on Monday after lunch | She salaried the bus to school this morning
